{
  "_id": "fhSubWhisperD001",
  "name": "Whisperdust",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A pale powder stirred into a drink. Modern street name for a recipe older than streets: the same blend of crushed seeds and synthetic alkaloids surfaces in every city's quieter corners under a different name each year. Users swear they can hear every whisper in a room.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 30 minutes you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Whisperdust (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Whisperdust.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws (background voices keep pulling at your attention).</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 12 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 5 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you have disadvantage on Wisdom and Intelligence saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 psychic damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 psychic damage and have the Incapacitated condition for 1 round.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can slip a dose into food or drink within 5 feet. A creature that consumes it is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances, such as a Pill Cutter or a Tincture Dropper.</em></p>"
    },
